<title>NIGERIA: Nigerian bourse closes to honour first president.</title>
<headline>Nigerian bourse closes to honour first president.</headline>
<dateline>LAGOS 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Nigerian stock market was closed on Wednesday because of a public holiday in Lagos in honour of the nation's first president Nnamdi Azikiwe.</p>
<p>Azikiwe died in May aged 91 and his body lay in state in Lagos on Wednesday as part of funeral rites that would lead to its final interment in eastern Nigeria on Saturday.</p>
